@startuml code-folding-state
title One fold range's collapsed/expanded state (per start_line)

[*] --> Expanded : fold_ranges() reports this range\n(EditorState::folded has no entry for it)

Expanded --> Collapsed : gutter arrow click\n(EditorState::toggle_fold)
Expanded --> Collapsed : CollapseFold (⌘−)\nwhen this is the innermost\nuncollapsed range at the caret

Collapsed --> Expanded : gutter arrow click again\n(EditorState::toggle_fold)
Collapsed --> Expanded : placeholder "⋯" click
Collapsed --> Expanded : ExpandFold (⌘+)\ncaret is on start_line\n(the only place it can be)

Expanded --> Collapsed : CollapseAllFolds (⌘⇧−)
Collapsed --> Expanded : ExpandAllFolds (⌘⇧+)

note right of Collapsed
  Interior lines (start_line+1..=end_line)
  are absent from VisualLines: no row,
  no caret, no click target. Only
  start_line itself still has a row,
  showing the "{ ⋯" placeholder.
end note

note left of Expanded
  An edit that removes this range from
  fold_ranges() (e.g. the brace pair no
  longer spans multiple lines) leaves a
  stale EditorState::folded entry inert --
  it simply stops affecting anything,
  rather than transitioning here.
end note
@enduml
